  "description": "meme-id: trump-can't-swing-it; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes an image of Donald Trump with a photo of a man in sunglasses, with the text 'trump can't swing it.' The visual pairing implies that Trump lacks the physical ability to swing a bat or perform a physical action, suggesting incompetence or weakness. While not explicitly targeting a protected group, the meme uses a physical disability metaphor (inability to swing) to mock Trump's perceived physical or athletic inadequacy. This can be considered harmful as it reduces a public figure to a physical caricature, potentially reinforcing stereotypes about physical ability being tied to competence or leadership. The meme's intent is to ridicule Trump through a visual pun, using the contrast between his image and the implied physical limitation to convey a message of mockery and undermine his perceived strength or capability.",
